{title: 438 - You Will See Your Lord A-Coming}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #438 • --- S.A.T.B. • 8.8.8.5}
{lyricist: Millennial Harp}
{composer: James White}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 438}
{meta: tune --- S.A.T.B.}
{meta: meter 8.8.8.5}
{meta: category Early Advent - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]You will [G]see your Lord acoming,
[D]You will see your [A7/E]Lord acoming,
[D]You will [G]see your Lord acoming
[D]In a few [A7]more [D]days.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D/A]Hear the band of music,
[A7]Hear the band of [D]music,
[A7]Hear the [D]band of music
[A7]which is sounding thro' the [D]air.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Gabriel [G]sounds his mighty [D]trumpet,
[D]Gabriel sounds his [A7/E]mighty [D]trumpet,
[D]Gabriel [G]sounds his mighty [D]trumpet
[D]In a few [A7]more [D]days.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]You will [G]see the saints arising,
[D]You will see the [A7/E]saints arising,
[D]You will [G]see the saints arising
[D]In a few [A7]more [D]days.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Angels [G]bear them to the [D]Savior,
[D]Angels bear them [A7/E]to the [D]Savior,
[D]Angels [G]bear them to the [D]Savior
[D]In a few [A7]more [D]days.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]Then we'll [G]shout, our suff'ring [D]over,
[D]Then we'll shout, our [A7/E]suff'ring [D]over,
[D]Then we'll [G]shout, our suff'ring [D]over
[D]In a few more [A7]days.</div>
{end_of_verse}
